      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn parts of a whole, units and proportional scaling.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If a known fraction of a whole is given, divide by that fraction to find the whole.\n\nIf 1/3 of a tank is 80 litres, whole tank = 80 ÷ 1/3 = 240 litres.\n\nThen any other fraction is easy to find.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
